$ Shallow-water propagation over a submerged bar with DCTA triads with the Saprykina biphase
$
$ Added for path coverage: no deck selected BIPHASE SAPR.
$
$ Note what the gauge table shows. SWDCTA scales its transfer with SIN(-BIPH),
$ and the Saprykina biphase 0.5*PI*(MIN(1.,DELL/PTRIAD(9))-1.) is exactly zero
$ over the whole regime DELL >= PTRIAD(9). REDTRIAD is therefore 0 at every
$ gauge here while the spectrum still differs from the triads-off run, because
$ the change arrives by transport from points further up the profile. That is a
$ property of the parameterisation, not a bookkeeping error -- the same
$ saturation that BF-17 describes for the asymmetry breaker index.
PROJECT 'TRIAD_BIPH_SAPR' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30.0 0.0 300 0 &
      SECTOR -10.0 10.0 20 0.10 2.0 31
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30 0 1.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.06 2.0 0.0 2.0

GEN3 WESTH
OFF WINDGROWTH
OFF WCAPPING
OFF QUADRUPLET
TRIAD DCTA BIPHASE SAPR

POINTS 'GAUGES' 2.0 0.0 10.0 0.0 15.0 0.0 18.0 0.0 &
         25.0 0.0 30.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'triad_biph_sapr.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'triad_biph_sapr.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 15.0 0.0 S1D 'triad_biph_sapr_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
